br([["12 Gave my god daughter, Joyce Walsh the younger, when she went home to Worcester from Heriford: 5s I sent to Mary Ansley, my neece, the same tyme: ls 10 Gave Mrs Elyzabeth Russell, som tyme my maid, Mrs Elyza 6 months usse for 100li, which I gave her to her", [90, 313, 1431, 264], [391, 360, 1516, 321], [391, 423, 1515, 377], [90, 478, 1321, 431], [87, 533, 1286, 486]], ["Russell mariage, due May 9, 1641: 4li 18 Gave Mrs Rogers\u2014l1s; fine thrid againe\u20144d: 16d Paid William Spencer for cariinge one waine loade of elme timber & one load of the crop from Ailston: 4s Adam For 2 loades of clay to new mend the clay chamber flore: 2s Stefens To Adam Stefens, 6 daies mendinge the ould chamber", [87, 588, 1522, 537], [91, 643, 1545, 597], [391, 698, 1234, 653], [391, 754, 1515, 708], [86, 808, 1515, 764], [88, 863, 1414, 816]], ["flores at John Fletchers howse, at 14d a day: 7s To his father in law, Baker, 6 daies making morter: 5s 6d Paid William Badam for putting a new sill in the stable walle: 6d For nailes\u20142d; for heare\u20144d\u2014to make morter for the stable walle: 6d For lether shreds to make [deletion] a whiting to wash", [390, 918, 1515, 874], [391, 973, 1573, 929], [391, 1028, 1310, 984], [392, 1075, 1521, 1039], [392, 1134, 1366, 1095], [391, 1185, 1522, 1149], [392, 1248, 1411, 1204]], ["the walles: 8d For a paier of stockings for James Wattis: 9d Elyza Gave Elyzabeth Acton to putt in her purce: Is Acton Bes Goulding and Anne Arnold spent in going 24\u201d to a woman to help her legge, wherof the woman had 10d: 18d To the smith in the Broad Streete for shuing my mares: 2s", [391, 1294, 1521, 1259], [392, 1357, 1521, 1315], [88, 1412, 1514, 1370], [88, 1467, 1280, 1423], [88, 1522, 1543, 1473], [391, 1577, 1514, 1534]], ["William For mending a bridle\u20143d; paid William Joyner & his Joyner 2 men 2 daies a peece at the pale in my upper gardin by the wo[o]dpile: 6s 6d Incke\u20141d; gave Mathias Rufford when he cam from Wiggmor\u2014ls: 13d Cobnalls Paid Thomas Abram & his partner for mowing mowed all the Cobnalls medows; 2 at 14d a day, a peece:\u201d! 12s", [87, 1632, 1402, 1580], [87, 1688, 1437, 1634], [391, 1741, 1572, 1699], [391, 1796, 1385, 1754], [390, 1855, 1543, 1805], [88, 1911, 1286, 1861], [87, 1961, 1536, 1918]], ["12s, hay Paid John Heane and his wyfe 3 daies making hay there: 3s 3d makers 9s 7d To John Morris, 3 daies\u20142s; William Rawlins, cantage of 2 daies\u20141s: 3s a To an ould man that loked work\u20144 daies making hay: 2s 4d To Joane Adiss, 2 daies making hay; 2 daies: Is", [91, 2015, 1571, 1968], [87, 2076, 1270, 2014], [87, 2117, 1513, 2068], [87, 2197, 1571, 2118], [390, 2235, 1513, 2193]], ["mowing, Paid Mr Henry Mellin, alderman of Heriford, for making and cariing 8 waine loades of hay from the Cobnalls to cariage ys Heriford: 20s 41s 7d Paid William Spencer for car[ry]ing 2 loades of the same hay: 5s Memrandon\u2014that the Widow Smith of Ewe Withington rents onfe] of the 3 pastures next her house, at 6li a yeare.", [87, 2294, 1334, 2246], [87, 2346, 1350, 2303], [86, 2405, 1535, 2351], [86, 2456, 1424, 2404], [389, 2515, 1512, 2466], [390, 2563, 1449, 2522], [390, 2621, 1446, 2577]], ["15li 9s 1d tru cast This date refers to the entry re Elyzabeth Acton.", [790, 2721, 1115, 2688], [85, 2814, 926, 2776]]]);
